suggests that the theoretical underpinnings of the observed correlations are still largely unresolved.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1111/j.1540-6261.1995.tb05184.x", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2012, 4, 30]], "date-time": "2012-04-30T13:48:13Z", "timestamp": 1335793693000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 4570, "title": ["What Do We Know about Capital Structure? Some Evidence from International Data"], "author": [{"given": "RAGHURAM G.", "family": "RAJAN", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "LUIGI", "family": "ZINGALES", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "container-title": ["The Journal of Finance"], "issued": {"date-parts": [[1995, 12]]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[1995, 12]]}}, {"DOI": "10.1016/0022-0531(76)90046-6", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2005, 2, 9]], "date-time": "2005-02-09T23:45:28Z", "timestamp": 1107992728000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 4479, "title": ["The arbitrage theory of capital asset pricing"], "author": [{"given": "Stephen A", "family": "Ross", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "container-title": ["Journal of Economic Theory"], "issued": {"date-parts": [[1976, 12]]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[1976, 12]]}}, {"DOI": "10.1111/j.1540-6261.1987.tb04565.x", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2012, 4, 30]], "date-time": "2012-04-30T06:28:53Z", "timestamp": 1335767333000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 4424, "title": ["A Simple Model of Capital Market Equilibrium with Incomplete Information"], "author": [{"given": "ROBERT C.", "family": "MERTON", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "container-title": ["The Journal of Finance"], "issued": {"date-parts": [[1987, 7]]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[1987, 7]]}}, {"abstract": "<jats:p>In Social Capital, Nan Lin explains the importance of using social connections and social relations in achieving goals. Social capital, or resources accessed through such connections and relations, is critical (along with human capital, or what a person or organization actually possesses) to individuals, social groups, organizations, and communities in obtaining their objectives. This book places social capital in the family of capital theories (the classical and neo-capital theories), articulates its elements and propositions, presents research programs, findings, and agenda, and theorizes its significance in various moments of interactions between individual actions and social structure (for example, the primordial groups, social exchanges, organizations, institutional transformations and cybernetworks). Nan Lin eloquently introduces a groundbreaking theory that forcefully argues and shows why it is 'who you know', as well as 'what you know' that makes a difference in life and society.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1017/cbo9780511815447", "type": "monograph", "created": {"date-parts": [[2012, 6, 19]], "date-time": "2012-06-19T12:55:26Z", "timestamp": 1340110526000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 4394, "title": ["Social Capital"], "author": [{"given": "Nan", "family": "Lin", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "issued": {"date-parts": [[2001, 1, 29]]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[2001, 1, 29]]}}, {"DOI": "10.1111/j.1540-6261.1964.tb02865.x", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2012, 4, 30]], "date-time": "2012-04-30T15:52:38Z", "timestamp": 1335801158000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 4318, "title": ["CAPITAL ASSET PRICES: A THEORY OF MARKET EQUILIBRIUM UNDER CONDITIONS OF RISK*"], "author": [{"given": "William F.", "family": "Sharpe", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "container-title": ["The Journal of Finance"], "issued": {"date-